    "tacticalNote": "Ancelotti's 4-2-3-1 gives Vinícius the freedom to run at defenders while Savinho provides pace and directness on the opposite flank. Bruno Guimarães and a partner screen the defense while the number 10 connects midfield to attack. Brazil wants to control possession but can also explode in transition — the two modes are deliberately blended.",
    "strength": "Individual quality at every position — Brazil has arguably more stars on the field at once than any other squad in the tournament.",
    "vulnerability": "Defensive concentration in high-pressure moments — Brazil's backline can be disorganized when pressed by direct, fast opponents, as Qatar 2022 showed."
